---
import DocsLayout from "../../../components/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";

const connectSignature = `connect(options: ClientOptions): Promise<MdbaseClient>

interface ClientOptions {
  connector: Connector;
  app: { name: string; version: string };
  timezone?: string;              // IANA zone for writes and queries; default: the host's
  features?: string[];            // optional features to request, such as "presence"
  reconnect?: false | { minDelayMs?: number; maxDelayMs?: number }; // on by default
  waitForDevice?: boolean;        // Private: wait for a device instead of failing
  onWaiting?: (why: MdbaseError) => void;
  signal?: AbortSignal;
}`;

const writeOptions = `interface WriteOptions {
  mutationId?: string;            // default: a new UUIDv7
  conflictMode?: "record" | "reject";
  timezone?: string;
  include?: Include;
  dryRun?: boolean;
  wait?: "pending" | "confirmed" | "published";
  signal?: AbortSignal;
}`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="API reference"
  description="A compact reference for @mdbase-dev/sdk: connect, the client, writes, status, files and errors."
  active="api"
  headings={[
    { href: "#constructor", label: "connect()" },
    { href: "#client", label: "Reads" },
    { href: "#operations", label: "Writes" },
    { href: "#connection", label: "Status and link" },
    { href: "#records", label: "Holds and conflicts" },
    { href: "#files", label: "Files" },
    { href: "#session", label: "createMdbase" },
    { href: "#notifications", label: "Other exports" },
    { href: "#errors", label: "Errors" }
  ]}
>
  <p>
    This page lists the main public API. The package’s TypeScript declarations
    are the full reference.
  </p>

  <h2 id="constructor">connect()</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={connectSignature} language="ts" label="Signature" />
  <p>
    Connectors: <code>relayConnector</code> and
    {" "}<code>nextRelayConnector</code> (remote, through the relay or to the
    hosted replica), <code>inProcessConnector</code>,
    {" "}<code>localLinkConnector</code>, and from
    {" "}<code>@mdbase-dev/sdk/node</code>, <code>ipcConnector</code> and
    {" "}<code>connectDaemonLocalhost</code>. In tests,
    {" "}<code>new MemoryReplica().connector()</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="client">Reads</h2>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Method</th><th>Returns</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>get(ref, include?, signal?)</code></td><td><code>RecordView</code>; throws <code>not_found</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>find(ref, include?, signal?)</code></td><td><code>RecordView | null</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>readMany(refs, …)</code></td><td>Several records in one call</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>query(query, include?, signal?)</code></td><td>One <code>QueryResult</code> page; <code>cursor</code> when there is more</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>pages(query, include?, signal?, &#123; onReset &#125;)</code></td><td>An async iterator over every page</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>live(query, include?)</code></td><td>A <code>LiveQuery</code>: <code>records</code>, <code>stale</code>, <code>complete</code>, <code>ready</code>, <code>subscribe(fn)</code>, <code>setQuery(q)</code>, <code>close()</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>changes(cursor?, limit?)</code></td><td><code>&#123; changes, cursor, reset &#125;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>watchChanges(cursor, onChanges)</code></td><td>A stop function with <code>ready</code> and <code>state</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>backlinks(…)</code></td><td>Records that link to a record</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>describe()</code></td><td>Types, contracts and settings of the collection</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>queryContract(&#123; id, version &#125;, options?)</code></td><td>Records through a contract’s field names</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>validate(refs?)</code></td><td>Validation issues per record</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>views.list()</code>, <code>views.execute(…)</code></td><td>Saved views</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    A <code>RecordRef</code> is a record ID, <code>&#123; path &#125;</code>,
    or a <code>RecordView</code>. <code>Include</code> is
    {" "}<code>&#123; body, effective, document, links, diagnostics &#125;</code>,
    each a boolean.
  </p>

  <h2 id="operations">Writes</h2>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Method</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>create(&#123; id?, type?, path?, frontmatter?, body?, document? &#125;, options?)</code></td><td>The ID is minted locally and usable at once</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>update(ref, &#123; patch, unset, add, remove, body, bodyEdits, ifRevision &#125;, options?)</code></td><td>Pass a <code>RecordView</code> to merge field by field</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>replaceDocument(ref, source, options?)</code></td><td>Replace the whole Markdown source</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>rename(view, to, &#123; updateRefs, ifRevision &#125;)</code></td><td><code>updateRefs</code> defaults to <code>true</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>delete(ref, &#123; ifRevision &#125;)</code></td><td></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>preflightRename(view, to)</code>, <code>preflightDelete(ref)</code></td><td>What the change would touch</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>receipt(mutationId)</code>, <code>awaitReceipt(mutationId, timeoutMs?)</code></td><td>The current receipt; or wait until it leaves <code>pending</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>pendingWrites()</code></td><td>Writes still waiting</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>records.open(ref, &#123; autosave, timeoutMs, signal, recovery &#125;)</code></td><td>A record session lease; see <a href="/sdk/editing/">Editing records</a></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <CodeBlock code={writeOptions} language="ts" label="WriteOptions" />
  <p>
    Every write resolves to a <code>Write</code>:
    {" "}<code>state</code>, <code>receipt</code>, <code>records</code> (the
    optimistic view), <code>mutationId</code>, <code>onReceipt(fn)</code>,
    {" "}<code>confirmed</code> and <code>published</code> (promises).
    {" "}<code>confirmed</code> rejects with an <code>MdbaseError</code> if the
    write is rejected or its outcome is unknown. <code>published</code>
    {" "}settles when a file-backed replica has written the change to disk,
    which can be before confirmation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="connection">Status and link</h2>
  <table class="api-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Member</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>getStatus()</code>, <code>onStatus(fn)</code>, <code>status</code></td><td><code>SyncStatus</code>: <code>mode</code>, <code>confirmedThrough</code>, <code>headKnown</code>, <code>pending</code>, <code>holds</code>, <code>unresolved</code>, <code>connection</code>, <code>installing</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>summarizeStatus(status)</code></td><td><code>&#123; kind, text, pending, holds, conflicts, confirmedThrough &#125;</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>link</code>, <code>onLink(fn)</code></td><td><code>"open"</code>, <code>"reconnecting"</code> or <code>"closed"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>hello</code></td><td>What the replica reported at connect, including the grant’s role and capabilities</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>close()</code></td><td>Close the client and its subscriptions</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

